# LibrePhotos — follow-ups (local fork / GPU deploy)

## Done (recent — verify in UI, then commit)

- [x] **Social graph Phase 1:** `photo_count` / link `weight`, D3 layout, node size & edge thickness, color tiers (gray/teal/blue/red), legend, always-visible labels
- [x] **Social graph Phase 2:** min shared photos slider (1–1500), highlight person search, hover tooltips; filter + graph tests (`SocialGraph.test.ts`)
- [x] **Social graph backend:** `social_graph.py` dedupe per photo/person in SQL; mount in `docker-compose.override.yml`
- [x] **Face dedupe:** one label per person per photo (`face_person_deduplication.py`); confirmed + inferred cleanup via `dedupe_face_person_labels`; dry-run then live run for `abubakar` (454 confirmed + ~12k inferred groups)
- [x] **Photo detail People list:** confirmed names top, inferred middle, “Who is this?” bottom (`PeopleSection` + `photos.py` serializer)
- [x] **Docs:** `statistics.md` (social graph), `face-recognition.md` (one person per photo)
- [ ] **GPU gaps:** bind-mount `views/faces.py` (or ship image) so label API auto-dedupes; bind-mount `serializers/photos.py` if API sort should apply without frontend-only sort

